It's because he's a skeleton.

270
00:20:00,280 --> 00:20:03,277
He doesn't have any blood
to drink, so they left him.

271
00:20:03,360 --> 00:20:05,357
Do you think they'll drink my cola too?

272
00:20:05,440 --> 00:20:06,440
Both of you!

273
00:20:06,920 --> 00:20:07,840
Shut up!

274
00:20:08,280 --> 00:20:09,320
May I speak?

275
00:20:10,980 --> 00:20:12,760
Wait, who is that?

276
00:20:13,980 --> 00:20:15,177
Sure, wasn't me?

277
00:20:15,260 --> 00:20:16,820
Show yourself, bro!

278
00:20:17,780 --> 00:20:19,597
I know not from where you hail.

279
00:20:19,680 --> 00:20:21,197
But if you're proficient in puzzles?

280
00:20:21,280 --> 00:20:23,720
I have one in the form of my head.

281
00:20:27,040 --> 00:20:29,780
I think this thing is talking to us.

282
00:20:31,640 --> 00:20:33,800
But what the heck is it?

283
00:20:34,480 --> 00:20:36,060
I am no thing

284
00:20:39,600 --> 00:20:40,760
Is it a bug?

285
00:20:41,020 --> 00:20:42,280
But it talks.

286
00:20:43,040 --> 00:20:44,920
Like a transponder snail?

287
00:20:45,300 --> 00:20:46,560
We're outnumbered.

288
00:20:46,660 --> 00:20:48,037
There are eight of them.

289
00:20:48,120 --> 00:20:49,840
I'm no insect either.

290
00:20:50,940 --> 00:20:54,940
That aside, it appears that you
people are trustworthy enough.

291
00:20:55,320 --> 00:20:58,320
What you see on the floor
are pieces of my face.

292
00:20:58,780 --> 00:21:02,000
I beg of you, please put
them back together for me.

293
00:21:02,540 --> 00:21:03,800
Your face?

294
00:21:04,140 --> 00:21:05,117
Wait, I see.

295
00:21:05,200 --> 00:21:06,340
It's a mouth.

296
00:21:06,580 --> 00:21:07,660
And an eye.

297
00:21:08,240 --> 00:21:09,260
How's this?

298
00:21:10,940 --> 00:21:12,120
There. Done.

299
00:21:12,460 --> 00:21:13,720
Yeah, that's a face.

300
00:21:14,120 --> 00:21:16,900
You left out a fair
number of parts, though.

301
00:21:18,620 --> 00:21:19,800
Let me try.

302
00:21:21,340 --> 00:21:22,170
Better?

303
00:21:22,740 --> 00:21:24,320
This doesn't feel right.

304
00:21:24,660 --> 00:21:25,560
No, no, no.

305
00:21:25,740 --> 00:21:27,446
Watch, this is how you do it.

306
00:21:29,040 --> 00:21:30,320
I dig that.

307
00:21:30,500 --> 00:21:31,820
I don't at all.

308
00:21:32,420 --> 00:21:33,657
Oh, let me try.

309
00:21:33,740 --> 00:21:35,440
This is my face.

310
00:21:35,700 --> 00:21:37,280
It's not a toy.

311
00:21:37,760 --> 00:21:38,700
Help me!

312
00:21:40,020 --> 00:21:41,340
I got it.

313
00:21:42,460 --> 00:21:44,200
Looking pretty human, bro.

314
00:21:45,660 --> 00:21:51,100
I believe my chin and hair may still
be somewhat awry, but it's good enough.

315
00:21:51,360 --> 00:21:52,200
I'm grateful.

316
00:21:53,720 --> 00:21:56,160
It's a severed head! Clearly.

317
00:21:56,800 --> 00:21:58,240
Wait, are you a ghost?

318
00:21:58,420 --> 00:21:59,460
How can you talk?

319
00:22:00,380 --> 00:22:01,797
I wish I knew that.

320
00:22:01,880 --> 00:22:05,060
A swordsman cut me into many pieces.

321
00:22:06,380 --> 00:22:10,340
That villain, he used
some manner of sorcery.

322
00:22:10,540 --> 00:22:13,020
He severed my limbs, but I did not bleed.

323
00:22:13,640 --> 00:22:14,600
I did not die.

324
00:22:15,020 --> 00:22:17,300
I was denied a warrior's death.

325
00:22:17,540 --> 00:22:19,599
Instead, I suffered this indignity.

326
00:22:20,280 --> 00:22:21,620
I'm a disgrace.

327
00:22:26,740 --> 00:22:28,600
One, two, three.

328
00:22:30,280 --> 00:22:31,110
Three.

329
00:22:31,193 --> 00:22:32,023
Four intruders.

330
00:22:38,980 --> 00:22:40,840
Well, did you find them?

331
00:22:41,360 --> 00:22:43,300
Yeah, they're right here.

332
00:22:43,500 --> 00:22:45,794
I've got all four of them in my sights.

333
00:22:45,920 --> 00:22:48,100
I'll take them out. Don't worry.

334
00:22:49,340 --> 00:22:50,180
I see.

335
00:22:53,000 --> 00:22:54,697
You have fun with that.

336
00:22:54,780 --> 00:22:57,740
Give me a ring when you're
done, all right? Roger.

337
00:23:13,080 --> 00:23:18,240
So this guy cut you you're
still alive even without a body.

338
00:23:18,500 --> 00:23:19,460
That's crazy

339
00:23:20,480 --> 00:23:22,560
It's like buggy creepy

340
00:23:23,520 --> 00:23:27,579
Under different circumstances, I'd
slit my belly and die and mourned.

341
00:23:27,900 --> 00:23:32,782
But alas, there's something that I must
do, even if I'm forced to live in disgrace!

342
00:23:40,660 --> 00:23:41,500
Hold on.

343
00:23:41,760 --> 00:23:44,717
Old man, can you tell us
anything about this place?

344
00:23:44,800 --> 00:23:45,940
Old man, you say?

345
00:23:46,200 --> 00:23:48,657
You need to show some respect, you woman!

346
00:23:48,740 --> 00:23:50,780
I'm a proud warrior, you know.

347
00:23:51,000 --> 00:23:54,300
Where I'm from, women are
chaste, and they are modest.

348
00:23:54,540 --> 00:23:57,540
They walk three steps behind the men. Huh?

349
00:24:01,020 --> 00:24:02,820
Too bad. I don't care.

350
00:24:03,120 --> 00:24:05,200
You're just a head. Be grateful.

351
00:24:05,480 --> 00:24:08,097
We easily could have kept
you in pieces on the floor.

352
00:24:08,180 --> 00:24:09,780
Unhand me, you damn harlot!

353
00:24:10,020 --> 00:24:12,196
Wow, you really don't get it, do you?

354
00:24:13,160 --> 00:24:15,500
I said unhand me! Curse you!

355
00:24:18,120 --> 00:24:20,660
Is this proper, where you come from?

356
00:24:21,220 --> 00:24:23,220
I've never suffered such rudeness.

357
00:24:24,420 --> 00:24:27,377
However, it seems your clothes
were torn from your body,

358
00:24:27,460 --> 00:24:29,813
so perhaps I should be more sympathetic.

359
00:24:32,260 --> 00:24:35,760
I chose this outfit myself,
thank you very much. What?

360
00:24:36,320 --> 00:24:37,900
Sorry, but I look good.

361
00:24:38,160 --> 00:24:39,513
Your attire is obscene.

362
00:24:40,180 --> 00:24:42,237
All you're wearing is a breast band.

363
00:24:42,320 --> 00:24:43,673
You like it, don't you?

364
00:24:44,400 --> 00:24:46,020
Yes, indeed I do.

365
00:24:46,300 --> 00:24:47,640
I know that look!

366
00:24:53,440 --> 00:24:54,800
You pervert!

367
00:25:07,200 --> 00:25:08,640
That was a trap!

368
00:25:08,980 --> 00:25:11,540
You must have cracked your skull!

369
00:25:11,800 --> 00:25:14,260
That looks painful! Yes! No!

370
00:25:14,760 --> 00:25:17,140
I mean, uh, it's fine.

371
00:25:17,540 --> 00:25:19,180
It barely tickles.

372
00:25:20,960 --> 00:25:21,857
I see.

373
00:25:21,940 --> 00:25:25,240
So a breast band is
appropriate in your land.

374
00:25:25,580 --> 00:25:26,480
I approve.

375
00:25:27,020 --> 00:25:28,637
I don't care what you think!

376
00:25:28,720 --> 00:25:30,661
Please, just answer me one thing.

377
00:25:30,920 --> 00:25:32,300
Who are you people?

378
00:25:32,680 --> 00:25:36,060
I heard our captors say that
you were seized from a ship.

379
00:25:36,920 --> 00:25:38,097
Yeah, that's right.

380
00:25:38,180 --> 00:25:39,180
We're pirates.

381
00:25:40,780 --> 00:25:41,980
You're pirates?

382
00:25:43,260 --> 00:25:45,520
If only I had known sooner!

383
00:25:47,640 --> 00:25:49,400
I loathe pirates!

384
00:25:49,760 --> 00:25:51,466
Though I should have guessed!

385
00:25:51,720 --> 00:25:53,661
That does explain your barbarism!

386
00:25:58,200 --> 00:26:02,820
In this frozen hell, I thought
we were all victims of fate.

387
00:26:03,160 --> 00:26:05,807
so I had hoped that we
could escape together.

388
00:26:06,700 --> 00:26:08,700
Alas, it shan't be so!

389
00:26:09,440 --> 00:26:10,270
Huh?

390
00:26:10,500 --> 00:26:12,137
Wait, you lost me here!

391
00:26:12,220 --> 00:26:13,640
What do you mean frozen?

392
00:26:13,960 --> 00:26:16,666
This place is so hot,
even the sea is on fire.

393
00:26:16,960 --> 00:26:19,077
Yeah, there was lava and everything.

394
00:26:19,160 --> 00:26:21,097
We were sweating just on the boat.

395
00:26:21,180 --> 00:26:22,460
Aha, I see.

396
00:26:25,640 --> 00:26:26,520
Old man?

397
00:26:29,180 --> 00:26:31,640
Did you see the volcano here?

398
00:26:31,860 --> 00:26:33,560
Or feel an eruption?

399
00:26:34,000 --> 00:26:35,176
Something like that?

400
00:26:36,000 --> 00:26:38,480
I did hear a loud explosion.

401
00:26:38,820 --> 00:26:42,291
But both the island and the
sea surrounding it were frozen.

402
00:26:43,260 --> 00:26:45,897
And that is the last
thing I shall say to you.

403
00:26:45,980 --> 00:26:46,900
Cursed pirates!

404
00:26:47,700 --> 00:26:48,530
The sky.

405
00:26:48,740 --> 00:26:50,387
I thought it looked strange.

406
00:26:51,240 --> 00:26:53,122
I could tell even from the boat.

407
00:26:54,120 --> 00:26:58,517
The flaming side that Luffy and the
others went to is only half of the island.

408
00:26:58,600 --> 00:27:03,071
The people that grabbed us took us to
the other side, which is frozen solid.

409
00:27:04,460 --> 00:27:06,197
We need to get out of this room.

410
00:27:06,280 --> 00:27:07,280
I don't care how.

411
00:27:07,440 --> 00:27:09,137
Then we'll find out what's going on here.

412
00:27:09,220 --> 00:27:13,817
I get what you're saying, but I kicked it
pretty hard, and that door isn't budding.

413
00:27:13,900 --> 00:27:15,140
Step aside! Huh?

414
00:27:15,760 --> 00:27:17,940
My cola is maxed out!

415
00:27:27,600 --> 00:27:29,540
Whoa, whoa, that's a big one!

416
00:27:32,220 --> 00:27:33,640
Ranking Radical Bee!

417
00:27:53,340 --> 00:27:55,740
Let's move, brother! Damn, Franky.

418
00:27:56,000 --> 00:27:57,717
Should have led with that one.

419
00:27:57,800 --> 00:28:00,180
Sometimes I wish I was a cyborg, too!

420
00:28:08,020 --> 00:28:09,540
So what are you gonna do?

421
00:28:12,020 --> 00:28:13,020
Last chance.

422
00:28:13,400 --> 00:28:17,165
You'd rather sit there on the
floor than associate with pirates?

423
00:28:17,960 --> 00:28:19,680
Silence! Leave me be!

424
00:28:20,300 --> 00:28:21,180
So what?

425
00:28:21,300 --> 00:28:24,829
Are you gonna roll out of here
and bite your way to freedom?

426
00:28:25,520 --> 00:28:26,780
Let me go!

427
00:28:28,980 --> 00:28:30,980
Well, Samurai, tell me!

428
00:28:31,980 --> 00:28:34,420
What? Samurai? For real?

429
00:28:35,640 --> 00:28:39,300
This topknot is a traditional
hairstyle in the land of Wano.

430
00:28:40,760 --> 00:28:43,200
So, he's the one who killed those guys?

431
00:28:43,420 --> 00:28:44,917
Does that mean he might kill us?

432
00:28:45,000 --> 00:28:46,760
Or bite us? No!

433
00:28:47,660 --> 00:28:49,072
What was that explosion?

434
00:28:49,300 --> 00:28:50,400
I have no idea.

435
00:28:50,640 --> 00:28:52,137
Do you think it was those pirates?

436
00:28:52,220 --> 00:28:53,520
Hey, they're coming.

437
00:28:53,700 --> 00:28:54,530
Let's hurry.

438
00:28:59,120 --> 00:29:03,980
We came here because we received a
distress call from one of your victims.

439
00:29:04,340 --> 00:29:07,060
You got a story you
want to tell us, or not?

440
00:29:07,420 --> 00:29:09,620
Sanji, come on! Leave him here!

441
00:29:09,880 --> 00:29:10,860
He's our enemy!

442
00:29:12,120 --> 00:29:16,860
I swear, I would not disgrace
myself by killing in cold blood!

443
00:29:20,080 --> 00:29:26,440
I'm here to save my son's life, and I
would cut down anyone who stands in my way!

444
00:29:35,460 --> 00:29:36,290
There!

445
00:29:36,373 --> 00:29:37,652
Don't let them get away!

446
00:29:43,640 --> 00:29:44,900
Those are my friends!

447
00:29:45,140 --> 00:29:46,316
Cut it out, will ya?

448
00:29:47,180 --> 00:29:48,100
Weapons left!

449
00:29:52,700 --> 00:29:53,980
You're kidding me!

450
00:29:54,200 --> 00:29:55,677
How did they get out of that room?

451
00:29:55,760 --> 00:29:58,740
I don't know, but we'd
better call the master.

452
00:29:59,500 --> 00:30:01,580
What the hell do they want from us?

453
00:30:02,340 --> 00:30:03,170
Dawn!

454
00:30:03,300 --> 00:30:04,360
Wait a sec!

455
00:30:04,800 --> 00:30:06,840
You brought the head? Why?

456
00:30:07,180 --> 00:30:09,260
It'll work out. Leave him to me.

457
00:30:13,640 --> 00:30:14,640
There's a door!

458
00:30:20,260 --> 00:30:21,090
What?

459
00:30:25,960 --> 00:30:27,020
Who are you?

460
00:30:28,340 --> 00:30:29,170
What?

461
00:30:32,040 --> 00:30:33,340
Hello there, kids.

462
00:30:34,180 --> 00:30:35,010
What?

463
00:30:35,093 --> 00:30:35,923
There's children?

464
00:30:36,006 --> 00:30:37,160
They're so big.

465
00:30:39,420 --> 00:30:41,140
I guess they're giants.

466
00:30:41,460 --> 00:30:44,060
But are we in prison or daycare?

467
00:30:44,240 --> 00:30:45,917
They're the biggest I've ever seen.

468
00:30:46,000 --> 00:30:48,437
Did we drop anchor on an island of giants?

469
00:30:48,520 --> 00:30:51,579
No, because they're are
regular-sized children, too.

470
00:30:51,720 --> 00:30:54,437
Okay, then it's some kind
of all-inclusive nursery?

471
00:30:54,520 --> 00:31:00,757
There aren't any adults here to
supervise, though, Mocha, who are they?

472
00:31:00,840 --> 00:31:02,720
I've never seen them before.

473
00:31:03,920 --> 00:31:05,817
You must be the ones who are frozen.

474
00:31:05,900 --> 00:31:08,097
How did you escape frozen?

475
00:31:08,180 --> 00:31:10,060
What is she talking about?

476
00:31:24,520 --> 00:31:25,350
Robots, huh?

477
00:31:26,200 --> 00:31:27,760
Whoa, are you okay?

478
00:31:33,720 --> 00:31:36,240
Oh man, these tykes really love me!

479
00:31:36,740 --> 00:31:39,328
And it's all because
of my armored physique!

480
00:31:40,760 --> 00:31:43,540
What did she mean by the
ones who were frozen?

481
00:31:44,480 --> 00:31:46,200
Look, a plushie!

482
00:31:46,640 --> 00:31:48,060
A stuffed raccoon!

483
00:31:48,380 --> 00:31:50,860
I'm a reindeer, okay? Too tiny!

484
00:31:51,640 --> 00:31:54,980
And cute! Yeah! Help! They got me!

485
00:31:55,120 --> 00:31:56,160
Close call.

486
00:31:56,560 --> 00:31:58,854
Sure glad they're not interested in me.

487
00:32:00,160 --> 00:32:00,990
Look!

488
00:32:01,140 --> 00:32:02,660
His eyebrow's curly!

489
00:32:03,000 --> 00:32:04,580
Shut up, small fry!

490
00:32:04,940 --> 00:32:06,100
It's freaky!

491
00:32:08,980 --> 00:32:10,820
That's it! I've had enough!

492
00:32:13,440 --> 00:32:15,860
Do you know a child named Momonosuke?

493
00:32:16,440 --> 00:32:18,520
I am looking for my boy!

494
00:32:20,860 --> 00:32:21,820
I'm scared!

495
00:32:22,320 --> 00:32:23,720
I don't have to talk!

496
00:32:24,560 --> 00:32:25,390
Hey!

497
00:32:26,980 --> 00:32:27,810
Don't go!

498
00:32:27,900 --> 00:32:29,017
We've got questions about the...

499
00:32:29,100 --> 00:32:30,040
Come back here!

500
00:32:30,860 --> 00:32:32,280
Hey! Shut up!

501
00:32:32,500 --> 00:32:34,457
We're trying to get
information out of them!

502
00:32:34,540 --> 00:32:36,775
And they won't talk if you scare them!

503
00:32:38,020 --> 00:32:40,196
The door to the biscuit room is open.

504
00:32:40,360 --> 00:32:41,497
They're coming for us.

505
00:32:41,580 --> 00:32:42,580
Let's get moving.

506
00:32:44,280 --> 00:32:45,751
It must be those pirates.

507
00:32:46,020 --> 00:32:47,608
We can't let them get away.

508
00:32:55,260 --> 00:32:57,540
What kind of facility is this place?

509
00:32:57,740 --> 00:32:58,937
You've got to tell us!

510
00:32:59,020 --> 00:33:01,608
You must aid me in my
search for Momonosuke!

511
00:33:02,600 --> 00:33:05,157
I thought we told you
to keep your mouth shut!

512
00:33:05,240 --> 00:33:07,057
I've been disgraced as a samurai!

513
00:33:07,140 --> 00:33:10,540
All because I was
attacked by a woman! What?

514
00:33:10,820 --> 00:33:13,291
Oh, quit your whining, you chauvinist pig!

515
00:33:13,380 --> 00:33:15,280
I knew it was them! I got them.

516
00:33:18,900 --> 00:33:19,730
No, wait!

517
00:33:20,400 --> 00:33:21,282
Hold your fire!

518
00:33:21,540 --> 00:33:26,128
We can't use guns or explosives, and
let's keep the gas grenades to a minimum.

519
00:33:28,340 --> 00:33:32,281
The master would be furious if we
were to hurt one of the children.

520
00:33:39,340 --> 00:33:42,397
Be good, little boys and
girls, and stay out of our way.

521
00:33:42,480 --> 00:33:44,317
If you don't, you might get hurt.

522
00:33:44,400 --> 00:33:45,635
It's dangerous, kids.

523
00:33:46,200 --> 00:33:47,030
Hey, Mr.

524
00:33:47,113 --> 00:33:49,077
Robot, did you come
from outside the island?

525
00:33:49,160 --> 00:33:50,600
Yep, I sure did, buddy.

526
00:33:51,120 --> 00:33:53,960
But let's be clear, I'm really a cyborg.

527
00:33:54,080 --> 00:33:55,077
Do you have a ship, right?

528
00:33:55,160 --> 00:33:55,990
Do we ever?

529
00:33:56,220 --> 00:34:00,000
It's called the Sunny. It's
the best. Then save us. Huh?

530
00:34:00,980 --> 00:34:02,509
What does he mean by that?

531
00:34:02,780 --> 00:34:05,800
You have to. Please. What do you mean?

532
00:34:05,940 --> 00:34:07,177
Take your kids with us?

533
00:34:07,260 --> 00:34:09,436
This place isn't a daycare after all.

534
00:34:09,800 --> 00:34:11,100
No, don't leave.

535
00:34:11,340 --> 00:34:12,516
Don't leave us here.

536
00:34:12,620 --> 00:34:16,640
We're not sick anymore. We're
better. Promise. What's that?

537
00:34:17,340 --> 00:34:18,400
They were sick?

538
00:34:27,160 --> 00:34:28,807
Damn it, they're in the way!

539
00:34:29,000 --> 00:34:30,320
Don't leave us behind!

